course: dictionary
lesson: 13076
title: Telling fibs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fibbing means telling small lies, usually about things that do not matter very much. Someone who fibs is a fibber. «Did you eat the last biscuit?» «No, I didn't.» If the answer is untrue, that is fibbing.
explain: Fib is a softer word than lie, but a fib is still not the truth. «Stop fibbing, Sam, I saw you take the cake.» The word tells you Sam is not being honest about something small.
explain: Fibbing is one form of the word fib: fib, fibs, fibbed, fibbing. Use fibbing when it is happening now: «He is fibbing about his homework.» Use fibbed for the past: «She fibbed about being ill.»
fact: Fibbing means telling small lies, usually about unimportant things.
fact: A fibber is someone who tells fibs.
fact: Fib is an informal word, often heard in playgrounds and at home.
fact: Fib sounds softer than lie, but a fib is still not telling the truth.
fact: Common phrases: «stop fibbing», «are you fibbing?», «a little fib».
exercise: «Ella said she had done her homework, but she had not.» What is Ella doing? | Reading aloud | Singing | Swimming | *Fibbing
exercise: Which word means someone who tells fibs? | Fisher | Fiddler | Firework | *Fibber
exercise: «Stop fibbing, Max, I saw you eat the last biscuit.» What does fibbing mean here? | *Telling a small lie | Painting a picture | Running very fast | Singing a silly song
test: Which word is the past form of fib? | Fizzed | Fibbing | *Fibbed | Fibs
test: What does «Are you fibbing about the time?» ask? | Whether it is time for lunch | Whether the clock is working | *Whether someone is telling a small untruth | Whether someone is singing
exam: Which sentence shows someone fibbing? | «Sam gave the jam to his gran.» | «Sam ran to the shop for milk.» | «Sam read a book about jam.» | *«Sam said he had not touched the jam, but there was jam on his face.»
